  "content": {
   "rendered": "\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Resident Days celebrate you, the people who make Edinburgh legendary. On specially chosen dates, residents with an EH postcode can enjoy free or discounted entry to a range of top attractions, tours, and hidden gems across the city, thanks to our partnerships with some of Edinburgh’s finest venues as part of the Resident Rewards programme</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Running across four key dates in 2026</strong>, choose to learn more about Scotland’s national drink, explore one of the oldest buildings on the Royal Mile, enjoy a round of golf, or limber up at a fitness class. Whichever one you decide on, it’s a fantastic way to enjoy our city’s unique culture, all while saving you a few pennies.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Please note, all offers are available exclusively to residents with an EH postcode. Some offers have a restricted number of tickets available, so early booking is advised.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-light-sandstone-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-light-sandstone-background-color has-background\"/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-primary-color has-text-color has-link-color has-large-font-size wp-elements-9\">2026 Resident Days:</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>World Heritage Day</strong> &#8211; 18 April 2026</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>World Tourism Day </strong>&#8211; 27 September 2026</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Silver Sunday</strong> &#8211; 04 October 2026</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>World Children&#8217;s Day</strong> &#8211; 20 November 2026</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-light-sandstone-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-light-sandstone-background-color has-background\"/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-primary-color has-text-color has-large-font-size\">Current Resident Days</h2>\n\n\n<div class=\"\">\n\n\t\t\n\t<div